# Android emulator media testing

## Don't record video on an emulator

Recording a video with the in-app camera (`CameraCaptureModal`, which calls expo-camera's
`recordAsync`) crashes the Android emulator itself on this Mac (qemu exits with code 139) the
moment recording starts. It happens with and without microphone permission. It is an emulator
bug, not an app bug, so don't retry it or debug the app for it. Video recording can only be
tested on a real phone.

## Test the video path through the library instead

Picking a video from the library, uploading it, and playing it back all work on emulators:

```sh
ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "testsrc=duration=3:size=720x1280:rate=30" -pix_fmt yuv420p clip.mp4
ffmpeg -f lavfi -i "testsrc=duration=8:size=720x1280:rate=30" -pix_fmt yuv420p long-clip.mp4
adb -s <device> push clip.mp4 /sdcard/Movies/clip.mp4
adb -s <device> shell content call --uri content://media/external/file \
  --method scan_file --arg /sdcard/Movies/clip.mp4
```

Then tap Library in a ritual answer or capsule and pick the clip. The 8-second clip should be
refused with "That video is longer than 5 seconds, so it wasn't added."

## Emulator photos are black

Photos taken with the emulator's camera come out black with a yellow timestamp. That's how the
emulated camera captures stills; the upload and display pipeline is working.

See `.maestro/README.md` (Native Coverage Still Manual) for what else needs a real device.
